# Wait for load

A browser step is FAIL only after loading signals are gone and the expected result is still missing. A slow Live Test is not a failure.

Treat these as still loading:

- a visible spinner
- the text "Loading", "Loading assistant", or "Nothing here yet"
- an empty reply bubble while Trace is empty
- a preview panel that still says the agent is loading

Before recording FAIL, poll about every 2 seconds. Do not mark FAIL on the first empty observation. After the last loading signal disappears, keep checking the expected result. Bound the wait at about 90 seconds so a real failure can still be recorded.

```text
Reply with Hello there!: PASS
  The reply arrived after the preview finished loading.
```

If a loading signal is still on the page at the time limit, do not record FAIL.
